From a2a9ed3dfc11e484b6b9598c4dfb0aabbe02e63c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <MiaAI-Lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 18:02:16 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] MiniMax-M3.1-Flash: dspark draft, device half (task 0017)

Taps after layers 3, 17, 31, 45, 59 in the forward (bf16 rows, per-slot window rows), the
draft's CUDA kernels (minimax_m3_dspark.cu: tap, add, norm, block heads, ring put, block
attention, top-C, Markov chain and confidence) with contract entries, launch records and
host twins with planted mutants, the draft's device pass (mxfp8/bf16 lane matmuls, per-stream
K/V rings, snapshots with the prompt cache), the engine/follower/lanes plumbing (Kind.absorb,
draft, snap; prepare_features/features/prefill_features), --drafter for the family
(dspark folder resolution, budget, fingerprint), steps test-minimax-dspark-dev and
test-minimax-dspark-kernels, tf-cuda-test mm3-dspark-contract / mm3-dspark-bench /
mm3-dspark-pass. Drafted decode equals plain decode on the host fakes; kernels pass gates 1-4
on spark1 and spark2; the pass matches float64 on synthetic weights on spark1. No run with
the real weights: acceptance and speed are NOT MEASURED.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
